  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 242 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nThe rain is expected to shut off by Friday afternoon as a cold front \nexits the area, but we may still be feeling this system's impacts \nnext week. Upstream rain traversing the Mississippi River is \nforecast to make it into the CWA late this weekend and to Chester by \nnext weekend. This has the potential to cause minor flooding at \nmultiple points, but exactly where and when the points crest remain \nto be seen.\n\nOtherwise, cooler and drier air will drive into the region behind \nthe cold front. High temperatures between Thursday and Friday could \ndrop as much as 15-20 degrees for most of the area east of I-55 in \nIllinois and south of I-44 (~90 degrees to ~70 degrees). Low \ntemperatures will feel the shift, too, albeit slightly more \ngradually. Expect widespread lows in the 40s and 50s by Friday \nnight. The change of pace is expected to last, too. The NBM IQR \nshows highs comfortably in the 70s through early next week. Even its \n75th percentile stays in the 70s for the majority of the period. \nRain will be all but a ghost as well, as the LREF 24 probs of a \ntrace of rain peak at 15% through next Thursday.",
